course: dictionary
lesson: 14697
title: The priesthood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The priesthood is a church word. It can mean the job of being a priest, or all the priests of a church or religion together. Look at the words around it for clues. «Sam felt called to the priesthood, so he went to a seminary to train.» A seminary is a school for training priests, so the priesthood must mean the job of being a priest.
explain: Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. «The priesthood of the old temple served the people for many years.» Priests served in a temple, so here the priesthood means the group of priests together.
explain: Christians say «the priesthood of all believers». The words all believers are the clue: this is not only about priests, but about every person who believes. It means every believer can speak to God directly.
explain: When context is not enough, use a dictionary. Priesthood is a noun, and it is usually used with «the», as in «the priesthood».
fact: «Priesthood» means the job and calling of being a priest.
fact: «Priesthood» can also mean all the priests of a church or religion together.
fact: Christians believe in «the priesthood of all believers»: every believer can speak to God directly.
fact: A seminary is a school where people train for the priesthood.
fact: «Priesthood» is a noun, and it is usually used with «the», as in «the priesthood».
exercise: «Ben decided to enter the priesthood after he left school.» What does priesthood mean here? | *The job of being a priest | Singing in a choir | A kind of old wooden church | A long holiday with friends
exercise: «The priesthood of the old temple served the people.» Does priesthood mean the job, or the priests together? | Only one priest | *The group of priests together | A school for children | A type of building
exercise: Christians say «the priesthood of all believers». Who can speak to God directly? | Only people who go to a seminary | *Every believer | Only the bishop | Nobody, only the church building
test: «Lily felt called to the priesthood.» What does called to the priesthood suggest? | *She felt she should become a priest | She was asked to play the organ at church | She had a bad day at school
test: «Tom trained for the priesthood at a seminary.» Where did Tom train? | *At a seminary | At a football club | At home, alone | At the beach
exam: Which sentence uses priesthood correctly? | Maria priesthood quickly ran home | Maria was very priesthood today | Maria priesthooded the cake for her friend | *Maria wanted a life in the priesthood
